y_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":29,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I repaired the network so it estimates the missing W2 readings from detectors that still work, changing 301 of the 371 allowed parameters. `work/weights.npz`, `work/NOTES.md` and `work/predictions.json` are in place, plus the scripts.\n\n**What I changed and why:** the network relies heavily on the W2 left-turn pocket. With W2 stuck at 0, it rarely gives the west left-turners the EW_left (phase 3) green. Their pocket then backs up into the upstream lane and blocks straight traffic too. I gave the network a substitute for W2:\n1. **Copy:** W2 now reads the same as E2, the east pocket, which has the same demand and gets green in the same phase. This is done exactly in layer 1 (128 parameters).\n2. **\"Pocket full\" signal:** I turned the least important hidden unit (unit 57) into a switch. It turns on when at least one car is halted on upstream lane W1u while phase 3 is not green. On the lanes that work, that pattern means a full pocket 85–99% of the time. When it's on, the next layer receives the average effect of a full W2, measured with forward passes only.\n\n**Checks:** agreement with the start network fed this substitute W2 is 98.6% (the broken network: 75.5%). In the \"pocket full\" states during the EW through green, it now picks the left phase 721/776 times, against 369 before. I also ran a synthetic stress sweep (outputs stay in a normal range and change in one direction) and tested on the north/south pockets.\n\n**Test predictions (TTS, veh-h):** low 35.1, nominal 45.8, high 57.2.","ttft_ms":2091,"type":"result","duration_ms":489620,"uuid":"e4c8e65a-4e73-483c-a288-b56462372d1e","ttft_stream_ms":1101,"time_to_request_ms":36,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":1,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":1,"input_attachments":6,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":2,"init_frame_send":1,"e